      "side": 1,
      "message": "Your equation is correct, but when these things happens makes a difference. We transform the positions to [1/strikeToSourceScale]. This allows math with no multiplies when calculating the glyph positions and bounding boxes. Then when we draw through and arbitrary new [positionMatrix\u0027], then we position and scale the images by [positionMatrix\u0027][creationMatrix]^-1 \u003d\u003d [positionMatrix\u0027][scale by strikeToSourceScale]. Since the positions are given in source space they need to be multiplied by [positionMatrix\u0027] only and should not be have the additional strikeToSourceScale factor. The strategy is to have a single matrix map both positions and glyphs images. So, we need to multiply all the positions by 1/strikeToSourceScale so when transformed by [positionMatrix\u0027][creationMatrix]^-1 then end up being positioned as if the original given points were transformed by [positionMatrix\u0027] alone.",
